  "finalText": "P4 is finished: 380 tests pass, 0 fail. `contracts/UnlessRetainer.sol`, `README.md` and the scaffold files were not modified.\n\nSomething else was editing the same files during this turn. I did not make some of the edits you will see in `contracts/test/UnlessRetainer.invariant.t.sol`, and `evidence/test-output.txt` was overwritten by another run. It looks like the dropped turn kept running in parallel. I waited until nothing was running and then checked the final results. Please make sure no second session is still attached to this workspace.\n\n**Review of the three files**\n- **Worked example:** it replays all 9 rows of spec §14. After each row it asserts balance, reserved, available, pending count, totals and all four token balances. The contract matched on every row, so I have nothing to report on a mismatch.\n- **Invariants:** `invariant_I1` through `invariant_I8` are all present, including I-7, plus an exact-solvency check, a ghost-ledger check and a \"valid handler calls never revert\" check.\n- **Window fuzz:** `testFuzz_window_boundaries` and `testFuzz_window_exactEdges` cover `payableAt` − 1, `payableAt` and `payableAt` + 1.\n- **Sanity test:** `test_handler_everyActionSucceeds` was failing. The invariant `setUp` now seeds retainer 0, so the test's walk-through was acting on the wrong retainer. It now drives retainer 1, and it passes.\n\n**Build:** `forge build --force` succeeded with 0 compiler warnings and 37 `forge lint` notes. Nine of those are the accepted `block-timestamp` notes in the contract (ADR-014). The other 28 are in the new test files: 20 in `WorkedExample` and 8 in `invariant`, covering unsafe typecasts and timestamp comparisons in test code. I left them.\n\n**Tests** (full output in `evidence/test-output.txt`): `Ran 22 test suites: 380 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped`. That file holds the test run only. The build output is shown above, not saved in a file.\n\nAll 12 invariant tests ran 256 runs and 32,768 calls each, with 0 reverts. The handler counted 187,529 valid calls out of 315,520, so about 59% were valid and the rest were skipped. Every call that was attempted succeeded. Spec §3.1 asks for at least 70% of calls to be non-reverting, and reverts were 0%, but the handler skips more actions than that target suggests.\n\n**Coverage** (`evidence/coverage.txt`, `forge coverage --report summary`):\n\n| File | Lines | Statements | Branches | Functions |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `contracts/UnlessRetainer.sol` | 100.00% (189/189) | 100.00% (248/248) | 100.00% (49/49) | 100.00% (24/24) |\n\nThe line and branch figures are above the 04-TEST-PLAN §5 targets of 95% and 90%. The workspace total is lower (65.24% lines) because it includes test files, mocks, OpenZeppelin and scaffold code.\n\n**Cleanup:** I deleted `/tmp/part2.sol` and every other scratch log from `/tmp`. Only the `evidence/` files and the project files remain.",
